    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "### Build an Undo History Stack\r\n\r\nThe Undo button should step back through each filter one at a time. To make that work, the app needs to remember what the state looked like *before* each filter was applied.\r\n\r\n`historyStack` is already set up for you — it's an array you can push snapshots onto and pop them off. A snapshot should capture everything the app needs to restore: the product list and the active filter pills. The tricky part is making sure your snapshot is a true copy of the state at that moment, not a reference to it.\r\n\r\nFigure out where in the code a snapshot should be saved, what it should contain, and how the undo button should use it.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Need help?</summary>\r\n\r\n**Example Prompts:**\r\n\r\n- \"How do I use a for loop to copy one array into another?\"\r\n- \"Why do I need to copy the arrays before pushing them to the stack?\"\r\n- \"How do I access the `items` property from the object I popped off the stack?\"\r\n- \"My Undo button works, but the filter pills aren't disappearing. What did I miss?\"\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n",
